From 481b748b7e79be705e5074af14a8a036bbda07cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:11:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Settings optimiser on 10 years of history, applied
 automatically

- Brings the walk-forward optimiser back, updated for the new rules:
  sizing method, time exit, turnover and sector filters, 8-week hold
  and climax sale join score, stop, profit level, trailing, buy zone,
  volume, market filter and breakout checks.
- Tunes on the older 70% of history, checks on the unseen recent 30%;
  only changes anything that made money in both periods within the
  drawdown limit and beat the current settings.
- Runs on up to 15 years (default 10). "Get 10 years of data" now
  downloads in ~1,900-day chunks (Kite's limit) plus a warm-up year.
- Applies the result automatically (optional), notifies, and keeps the
  previous settings for one-tap Undo.
- One-time history analysis kept compact (only what the simulation
  reads) and raw candles released after use, so 10 years of the Nifty
  500 fits a small server; worker gets a larger memory allowance.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013Q9VNStcDLsK2gtz6b8dww
